{
  "repository": "sv5byp/FTFlow",
  "tag": "r171",
  "title": "FTflow r171 - Full upgrade with RTTY and CW Bot",
  "body": "FTflow r171 is the full-package continuation of FTFlow, including the existing weak-signal modes plus RTTY Bot and CW Bot. Older releases remain available.\n\n### Download and migrate\nDownload **FTflow-SV5BYP-r171-Windows-x64-portable.zip**, extract the **complete ZIP** to a new folder and run **FTFlow.exe**. No setup/installer is required; disk and USB use are supported. Close the old instance, retain a backup of settings/logs and configure the radio/audio devices for your computer.\n\n**This is a full-package migration. Use the ZIP download, not the older program-only automatic updater.** The complete package includes the updated FTFlow-Time.exe, the local DeepCW model and automation runtime. Replacing only an EXE is insufficient. The older updater channel is retained for legacy releases while this full-package release is downloaded manually.\n\n### Included\n- RTTY Bot and CW Bot with editable F1-F12 messages, contest exchanges, ADIF/UDP logging and selected-station automatic QSO.\n- CW DSP, automatic/manual WPM, adjustable receive AFC and optional parallel multichannel text with decoded sender/recipient. A callsign click selects without transmitting.\n- Verified clock synchronization with independent before/after measurements and transmission guarding. **Automatic synchronization defaults OFF in a fresh profile; the user's ON/OFF choice is saved.** Windows10/11 and built-in Windows PowerShell5.1 are required for this optional feature. First activation may request Windows permission once.\n- DF tolerance asks once per continuous adjustment session; using another control/window/application starts a new confirmation session.\n\n309 automated software checks passed for r171. Validation used simulated clock correction and radio routes plus read-only NTP measurements. Actual privileged clock correction/task installation and physical radio/audio/CAT/PTT acceptance were not exercised during development.\n\nBased on MSHV by Hrisimir Hristov, LZ2HV; original credits, map attribution and GNU GPL license are retained. The DeepCW model by VE3NEA is MIT-licensed with attribution included; no proprietary CW Skimmer decoder is included. The source ZIP provides the corresponding source. SHA256SUMS.txt contains archive checksums.\n",
